<title>USA: Delta Air Lines CEO Allen to retire.</title>
<headline>Delta Air Lines CEO Allen to retire.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delta Air Lines Inc said Monday its chief executive officer, chairman and president, Ronald Allen, announced his retirement, effective July 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The company said Allen will also resign from the board of directors.</p>
<p>Allen will work with the board to find a successor and will stay on as a consultant and advisory director, it said.</p>
<p>Delta also said it named Maurice Worth, currently executive vice president of customer service, as acting chief operating officer.</p>
</text>
